 ### Naive Combination Baseline (DVGO-NeuS)
-A straightforward combination of DVGO and NeuS, replacing the volume rendering in DVGO with the SDF-based volume rendering scheme. It serves as the naive baseline in this work, which can hardly produce satisfactory results [S4, unofficial]. In the baseline model, the color network tends to depend more on the additional under-constrained voxel feature grid input, thus breaking color-geometry dependency. Additionally, due to a high degree of freedom in optimizing a voxel grid, it is hard to maintain a globally coherent shape without additional constraints [S4, unofficial].
